#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:123
msgid "Flatpak"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:124
msgid ""
"We also have Flatpak for nightlies and stable builds, these builds are not mai"
"ntained by the core developers themselves. You can either get the builds from "
"the `KDE community website <https://binary-factory.kde.org>`_ or from the `Fla"
"thub Maintainers <https://flathub.org/apps/details/org.kde.krita>`_. The KDE c"
"ommunity website only offers nightly builds of Flatpak."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:126
msgid ""
"To install Flatpak build from the software center just open the Flatpakrepo fi"
"les with Discover or the software center provided by your distribution:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:128
msgid "`Flathub Repo <https://flathub.org/repo/flathub.flatpakrepo>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:130
msgid "`KDE Flatpak Repo <https://distribute.kde.org/kdeapps.flatpakrepo>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:132
msgid ""
"After adding one of the above repos you can then search for Krita and the soft"
"ware center will show you the Flatpak version for installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:134
msgid ""
"If you prefer doing it from terminal you can use the following commands to ins"
"tall Krita's Flatpak build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:136
msgid "For KDE Flatpak Repo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:138
msgid ""
"``flatpak --user remote-add --if-not-exists kdeapps --from https://distribute."
"kde.org/kdeapps.flatpakrepo``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:140
msgid "``flatpak --user install kdeapps org.kde.krita-nightly``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:142
msgid "For installing it from Flathub Repo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:144
msgid ""
"``flatpak --user remote-add --if-not-exists flathub https://flathub.org/repo/f"
"lathub.flatpakrepo``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:146
msgid "``flatpak --user install flathub org.kde.krita``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:149
msgid "Snaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:150
msgid ""
"There are snap packages provided by the Ubuntu snap developers, these are gene"
"rally not up to date. The Krita Developers do not provide or build the snap pa"
"ckages themselves. To install Krita as a snap package, first install snapd app"
"lication. Snapd is installed by default on Ubuntu distributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:152
msgid ""
"If you are on Ubuntu distribution then Krita's snap package may show up in the"
" software center, or you can run the following command in terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:154
msgid "``sudo snap install krita``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:158
msgid ""
"The Flatpak and Snap builds are not tested by the core developers of Krita, so"
" you may encounter some bugs while running Krita installed from them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:161
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:163
msgid ""
"You can download the latest binary from our `website <https://krita.org/downlo"
"ad/krita-desktop/>`__. The binaries work only with macOS version 10.12 and new"
"er."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:168
msgid "Source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:170
msgid ""
"While it is certainly more difficult to compile Krita from source than it is t"
"o install from prebuilt packages, there are certain advantages that might make"
" the effort worth it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:172
msgid ""
"You can follow the development of Krita on the foot. If you compile Krita regu"
"larly from the development repository, you will be able to play with all the n"
"ew features that the developers are working on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:173
msgid ""
"You can compile it optimized for your processor. Most pre-built packages are b"
"uilt for the lowest-common denominator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:174
msgid "You will be getting all the bug fixes as soon as possible as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:175
msgid ""
"You can help the developers by giving us your feedback on features as they are"
" being developed, and you can test bug fixes for us. This is hugely important,"
" which is why our regular testers get their name in the about box just like de"
"velopers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:177
msgid ""
"Of course, there are also some disadvantages: when building from the current d"
"evelopment source repository you also get all the unfinished features. It migh"
"t mean less stability for a while, or things shown in the user interface that "
"don't work. But in practice, there is seldom really bad instability, and if it"
" is, it's easy for you to go back to a revision that does work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/getting_started/installation.rst:179
msgid ""
"So... If you want to start compiling from source, begin with the latest build "
"instructions from the guide :ref:`here <building_krita>`."
msgstr ""

